when choosing a premium laptop you've  generally got a choice between a windows  machine and a macbook  with windows laptops usually offering  more performance and features  at a lower price point and that's the  case for huawei's matebook x pro  with the quad core processor 16  gigabytes of ram  a 3k touchscreen display 512 gigabytes  of nvme ssd storage  full speed thunderbolt 3 and a dedicated  graphics chip  you truly get a lot for your 1500 and  it's constantly on sale for  just thirteen hundred dollars and that's  why we're comparing it to apple's  thirteen hundred dollar  2017 13-inch macbook pro which is  constantly on sale for around twelve  hundred dollars  we've got links to those sales in the  video description below so we're going  to be comparing everything we can  between these laptops  but we'll focus on things that affect  your day-to-day experience  like the display keyboard trackpad  speakers and overall usability by far  the biggest thing that affects your  experience is the operating system  and if you like using windows 10 the  matebook x pro is the obvious choice for  what you get for the money  but there's a big market of people who  prefer mac os for reasons like better  reliability and higher resale value  and they're okay paying extra cash to  get it now for those who could really go  either way  let's compare both laptops and see which  laptop is better in each category  starting with exterior design the  matebook is slightly thicker near the  rear  but longer and thinner near the front  they both share a premium aluminum  design which was introduced by apple  many years ago  and the undersides look extremely  similar with cooling vents located away  from the bottom  so you can use it on your lap without  worrying about overheating  upon opening both laptops the matebook  almost looks like an exact copy of the  macbook  the truth is that it sucks for apple but  it's great for us consumers because the  design  is admittedly great with both laptops  looking so similar in design  it's gonna have to come down to the fine  details for the macbook to have a chance  of getting ahead  let's start with the displays from first  glance the matebooks display looks many  times better than the macbooks  the bezels are much thinner especially  at the top thanks to the relocation of  the webcam  literally built into a pop-up key on the  keyboard the resolution is higher  at 3k instead of 2.5 k and what i really  like about it is the very tall 3x2  aspect ratio  which is even taller than the macbook  macbook's 16x10 ratio  which gives you a lot more vertical  screen space compared to standard 16x9  which matters a lot for browsing the web  not only that but it's very color  accurate as well  with a 100 srgb coverage but the macbook  pro takes it further with dci p3 wide  color gamut  which covers 25 percent more color space  than srgb  the matebook also seems to lack contrast  with blacks looking a little bit gray  compared to deep blacks on the macbook  both displays are almost identical in  terms of maximum brightness  but the matebooks display is also a  touchscreen which can be nice to have  but we noticed that it's a bit more  reflective than the macbook pro  which can get a bit annoying in bright  conditions however i still think the  mate book wins out in the display  category for the near bezel-less design  and i think it was really clever to hide  the webcam to be able to achieve it  even though it makes for an unattractive  up the nose camera angle  i personally never use my macbook's  webcam anyway now let's get to the  keyboards  what you've heard about the macbook keys  is true they don't offer very much key  travel at  all the matebooks keys remind me of how  macbooks used to be  with substantially more key travel it  honestly just feels better to type on  the matebook  and you don't have to worry about the  dead key problem that macbooks have been  having which i personally haven't  experienced yet on any of the new  macbooks i've used  so i think it's a pretty rare problem  the matebook's power button doubles as a  fingerprint reader  which this model of the macbook pro  lacks to get touch id  you'll need to opt for the more  expensive touch bar model or a 2018  macbook air  before we test the speakers let's  compare the track pads  they look really similar with the  macbooks being slightly bigger  but apple uses force touch technology  which basically utilizes a motor beneath  the trackpad to simulate a click  click pressure is fully customizable and  you can press firmly after clicking once  to perform  additional options just like 3d touch on  recent iphones  the beauty of using this technology is  that you get an even clicking feel  all around the trackpad unlike the  matebooks trackpad  which is easy to click near the bottom  and almost unclickable near the top  the matebooks trackpad is still better  than most windows laptops out there  but the macbook pro easily wins in this  category now let's compare the speakers  starting with the sound comparison  [Applause]  [Music]  the few things i noticed is that the  highs were a lot better on the macbook  making it louder overall compared to the  matebook there wasn't much of a  difference in mids or bass  but the macbook sounds much more clear  compared to the mate book which sounds a  bit flat like various sound frequencies  are clashing together  so in almost every scenario the macbook  pro speaker sounded better  now let's quickly mention the ports both  get two usbc  ports with both of them on the macbook  pro supporting thunderbolt 3  and just one of them on the mate book  which also gets a usb a port which is  really convenient for using flash drives  and that port is missing on the macbook  with that said all that's left to  compare is specs and performance  you simply get so much more for your  money with the matebook a 4  core processor instead of a 2 core 16  gigabytes of ram compared to 8  512 gigabytes of ssd storage compared to  only 128 on the base macbook pro  so we recommend macbook users to get at  least 256 gigs  which brings the price up to 1500 and if  you're paying that much already  you may as well just pay 300 more for  the 2018 touch bar model instead  now the biggest difference is that the  matebook actually gets dedicated  graphics  which you can't get on the macbook pro  unless you opt for the 15 inch model  which starts at 2400 this was really  surprising to us and it puts the  matebook a step ahead  comparing geekbench 4 graphic scores the  difference in graphics performance is  significant  the quad core processor also destroys  the dual core on the macbook pro  especially in the real world cinebench  r15 cpu test  so what's the rundown which laptop is  the better choice  well if you don't mind using windows the  matebook x pro  is by far the better machine for your  money there are ways the macbook pro is  definitely better  but it's not nearly enough to top the  value of the matebook  and the best part is that it looks and  feels pretty similar to the macbook  with a much better display and keyboard  now if you own an iphone  apple watch maybe an ipad or a set of  earpods  you're gonna have a much better  experience with the macbook pro with all  the features you get with the apple  ecosystem  and macbooks generally tend to be more  reliable and age better compared to  windows laptops  so there's another factor to consider if  you plan on keeping your laptop for many  years but for the sake  of comparing the value of these two  laptops the matebook wins  if you enjoyed this comparison make sure  to hit that subscribe button above  because we're getting our hands on the  2019 imac really soon  and we'll be doing comparison videos on  that as well thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video
 

